WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.200
-Jason, I'm so happy
that you're here, but,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.501
we have to admit that you were

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:06.801
supposed to be
on "Stephen Colbert."

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:09.100
-You were not my first choice.
-Okay, I understand.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.501
-But I was yours,
and then you hit him in the neck

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:16.601
with a blow dart of COVID.
-Yes.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:17.767
-Right?
-Yes, yes.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.501
-So Colbert got COVID and...
-And you're here.

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:22.300
-...Jimmy said,
"Hey, I got him."

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.701
"Will you come over and play?"

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:27.767
-Stephen, get well soon.
We do love Stephen.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:30.334
-No, it was going to be like me

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:32.501
and Laura Linney
and Julia Garner.

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:33.767
We were going to go do that.
It was going to be like

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.234
a cast interview.

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:40.033
Julia Garner couldn't
get here from London,

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.501
Stephen got COVID,

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.934
and Laura, whatever.

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:46.100
-I'm always here for you.
I'm always here for you,

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.567
whenever you're around.
-It worked out perfect.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:49.400
-I, like, follow you around.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.901
I go, I just want to make sure
you're okay, man.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:53.100
You know I love my
Jason Bateman.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.501
I need my Jason Bateman.
-I love it.

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:55.934
-The world, we need --
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:59.968
We'll do anything
for the Jason Bateman.

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:02.968
-But here's the thing.
We got no plan.

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:05.300
-No, we don't know what we're
going to talk about.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.734
-We're just going
to free ball this, y'all.

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.133
-Are you left-handed?

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:13.434
-I am. Well, here's a deal.

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.167
See? We're already improvising,
guys.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.167
It's beautiful.

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:17.434
He's just doing visual cues.

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:18.667
I got my watch on this hand.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.367
So, yeah,
so I write with the left,

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:22.801
I throw with the right.
I kick with the left,

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:26.200
I eat lefty, I play pool lefty,

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.300
I golf righty, bat righty.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.667
I'm all messed up.
-Wow!

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:30.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:31.934
That is really
interesting to me.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.534
I did not know that.
-It's a problem.

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.601
-Yeah, but is it a talent?

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.234
Do your daughters
have this same talent?

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:38.467
Are they ambidextrous?

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.467
-I don't know if that's a
talent. I don't know

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.033
if left-handed
is being a talent.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.667
They are talented.
-Yes.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.834
But do they throw or they all --
-They don't.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.501
And, in fact, speaking of golf,

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:48.901
I took the 10-year-old --

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.868
two daughters, 15 and 10 --

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:53.367
Maple, the 10-year-old,
I took her out

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:55.567
because Daddy likes
to play some golf,

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.934
and she's like,
"Well, what, why?

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:00.501
What are you doing out there?
That looks terrible."

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:03.033
And I said,
"Well, come out and try it."

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.367
So I took her out to play golf.

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:06.734
She plays righty as well.

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:09.267
And she was just striping it.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.267
She's 10 years old
and I was like,

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:12.334
"Honey, here's the deal."

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:13.834
Because my wife hates golf.

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:16.033
My wife is like,
"What are you doing out there?

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.400
Think about all the housing,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.467
if you got rid of all the golf
courses," it's like that.

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:22.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.667
-That's so funny.
-So now I'm trying

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:26.801
to recruit Maple into the golf,
you know, addiction

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:29.133
because that means Daddy
can play a lot more golf.

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:30.934
We can travel.
I said, "Listen.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:33.701
You get great at this,
you get all hopped up about it,

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:37.033
you and I can have
Daddy-daughter time.

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:38.334
We can travel."
I said, "There's courses

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:40.667
in France and stuff like that."
You know.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:41.934
-Spend the rest of our lives
together.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:43.501
-Yeah.
Mommy and Franny will have fun.

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:44.801
doing whatever the hell
they want to do."

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.501
-[ Laughs ] In the house.
-"And you and I, we can fly

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.200
around the world!"
-Yes!

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.868
-So she's working on her swing.
-Yeah, she is, yeah.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.133
That's good.

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:56.501
You want that?
-I want it.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:58.100
-They're very cute kids.
I was very lucky,

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.467
I got to do your podcast,
"Smartless."

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:01.834
-Mm-hmm.
-And it was very funny.

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:04.534
-We originally -- well, we had
booked Stephen Colbert,

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:06.200
but then, he couldn't.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.901
-Yeah, because he got COVID.
-You see what I did there?

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.701
-He got COVID again, yeah,
exactly.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.868
I'm just making sure-
-Guy's lousy

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:14.400
with all kinds of viruses.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.000
-The way the podcast works,

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.267
if you don't know "Smartless" --

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:19.400
-Hold for applause.
[ No applause ]

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.801
-We'll add it in later.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.734
You can't hear it, but it's
getting a standing ovation.

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:25.934
-It's pretty solid.
-Yeah, it's pretty serious.

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:28.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:29.367
Too late. Too late.
-It is the best.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.334
No, it is so fun.
-Too late.

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:34.133
-But, basically,
it's you and two other hosts,

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:35.634
Sean Hayes and Will Arnett.

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:37.133
-Irrelevant.
-Irrelevant, yes.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:39.234
It doesn't matter. It's really
"The Jason Bateman Show."

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:40.534
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:42.267
One of you knows
who the guest is,

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.334
the other two do not.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.167
-Yeah.
We take turns inviting guests

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:47.901
and we don't tell the other two
who that guest is,

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:50.634
so that the other two
do not need to prepare.

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:53.234
See, we don't need to do stuff
like this. You know?

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:54.868
-Yeah.
-Jimmy's been up for hours,

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:58.300
you know, since he nailed that
dart into Stephen's neck.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.901
-Yeah, Colbert, yeah,
he's taking a day off.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:03.000
I want to make sure I get
these questions in, yeah.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.701
-Yeah, but we, you know,
we're -- actors are not

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:08.601
incredibly, should we say,
disciplined

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:09.968
with their work ethic.

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:12.634
So we like to have -- we don't
like to break a sweat.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:15.033
So I said --
Or maybe Will said --

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.968
Will thinks it's his idea.
I think it was my idea.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:19.534
That we don't tell the other
person who the guest is

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:21.000
so you don't have to do
any work.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.133
You literally just lift up the
laptop, boom, we're recording,

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:27.000
and you can just be there just
an observer,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.434
and, like, "Oh, my gosh, there's
Tom Hanks."

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:31.534
I've always wanted to ask
Tom Hanks this question.

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:34.334
And so it's very -- you know,
it's in real time,

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:35.901
like the listener would be.

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:37.534
You know? We're just --
-It's great.

00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:40.634
-Yeah. It's really fun
because we get to talk to people

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:44.334
that are heroes of ours
and you can skip,

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:46.033
you know, four or five dates.

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:47.334
You can just get right
into asking

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:48.901
like you're trapped
in an elevator with somebody.

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:50.400
-Yeah, but is there any times

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.033
where you're doing the interview
and you go,

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:54.334
"Ooh, I kind of wish
I knew that person was coming

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:57.968
so I could prepare"?
Like Paul McCartney.

00:04:57.968 --> 00:05:00.267
-Sean had Paul McCartney
was his guest...

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:03.467
[ Laughter and applause ]
...and, yeah, I was like --

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:05.901
Now, see, now the tepid applause
of Paul McCartney

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:08.501
makes me feel better about
no applause for "Smartless."

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.501
[ Laughter ]
-It wasn't tepid.

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:11.767
They weren't sure if they --

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:13.734
-The bar is down, yeah.

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:15.601
-They know that Paul McCartney's
not going to come out,

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:17.234
so they're just like,
"Yeah, yeah,

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:18.734
we love Paul McCartney,
but we know he's not there."

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:21.067
-If Paul McCartney
had a podcast, "Whoo!"

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.300
-No, no, no. They're like,
"Jason Bateman's here.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.267
Let's get to the Bateman,"
that kind of standing O.

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.067
-But, no -- yeah, so --

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:30.767
Yeah, if I knew
Paul McCartney was coming out,

00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:33.801
I would have been like,
you know --

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:37.367
because like, I love Wings --
-Me too.

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:38.534
-But the fact that he --

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:40.501
Did you know he was
in a band before that?

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:41.968
Like I had no idea.

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:45.567
So he comes out and I'm like --
I was a little embarrassed

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:47.601
because they start talking
about the Beatles.

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:48.834
-And you go, "I've never heard
of you."

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:50.334
-Well, there are no bugs
in my house.

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:51.734
What are you talking about?"

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:53.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.901
And so that was
embarrassing for him.

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:57.400
I wish I'd had a little bit
of a heads-up, yeah.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.834
-I want to talk about "Ozark."

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:02.801
It's the final season. It's
coming to an end. It's over.

00:06:02.801 --> 00:06:05.133
-This is it. Well, listen,
"all good things..."

00:06:05.133 --> 00:06:07.367
-Oh, it's great, yes.
It's a series final--

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.100
All good things,
all great things.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.801
This is one of the best shows
I've ever seen.

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:12.934
-Thank you, buddy.
-And, dude, you are so good...

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:14.300
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:18.267
-...in this. You are so good.

00:06:18.267 --> 00:06:20.267
I just don't want it to end.

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:22.067
But I heard this --
that, originally,

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:23.734
you weren't supposed
to be in it.

00:06:23.734 --> 00:06:26.167
You were just producing it
and directing.

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:30.234
-That was my original goal,
was to direct them all.

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:31.968
The acting part of it,
I can't remember

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:34.801
what the sequencing of it was,
but, yeah.

00:06:34.801 --> 00:06:37.434
I -- I, um -- I just --
I don't know what it --

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:39.400
maybe because I've been doing
so much comedy,

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.868
the idea of doing something dark
and dramatic

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.667
and then, especially
as a director, too,

00:06:43.667 --> 00:06:46.467
where, you know, you get
to shoot cinematic stuff

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:49.534
and like work with a composer
about creepy music

00:06:49.534 --> 00:06:52.100
and all that stuff
was really exciting to me.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.567
And the scripts were such
that it was like,

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:55.801
"Oh, yeah, you're going
to need to do that

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:57.834
to match these scripts
because they're dark."

00:06:57.834 --> 00:07:00.734
-Yeah.
-And so that was the plan.

00:07:00.734 --> 00:07:02.367
Couldn't make enough time
to direct them all,

00:07:02.367 --> 00:07:03.734
so I just did the first two
and the last two

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:05.901
of that first season
and did a bunch since then.

00:07:05.901 --> 00:07:07.567
-Yeah. I want to talk more
about "Ozark"

00:07:07.567 --> 00:07:09.601
when we come back
and also show a clip.

00:07:09.601 --> 00:07:10.834
More with Jason Bateman
after the break.

00:07:10.834 --> 00:07:11.834
Come on back.

